    <section class="rules">
      <h2>Rules & Guidelines</h2>
      
      <div class="rules-category">
        <h3>Team Formation</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Teams must consist of 1-4 members</li>
          <li>All team members should be from the same institution (recommended but not mandatory)</li>
          <li>One person can only be part of one team</li>
          <li>Team composition cannot be changed after registration closes</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="rules-category">
        <h3>Project Requirements</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Originality:</strong> All projects must be original work created during the hackathon</li>
          <li><strong>No Plagiarism:</strong> Using existing code or projects from previous hackathons is strictly prohibited</li>
          <li><strong>Open Source:</strong> Teams are encouraged to use open-source libraries and frameworks</li>
          <li><strong>Code Repository:</strong> All code must be hosted on GitHub and made public after the event</li>
          <li><strong>Documentation:</strong> Include README with setup instructions and project description</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="rules-category">
        <h3>Development Timeline</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>All work must be completed within the 24-hour hackathon window</li>
          <li>Pre-hackathon research and planning is allowed</li>
          <li>No pre-written code specific to your hackathon project</li>
          <li>Time tracking and activity logs may be verified</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="rules-category">
        <h3>Presentation & Demo</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Each team gets 10 minutes for final presentation (7 min pitch + 3 min Q&A)</li>
          <li>Live demo is mandatory – videos alone are not acceptable</li>
          <li>Presentation slides should be submitted 30 minutes before scheduled time</li>
          <li>All team members should be present during the presentation</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="rules-category">
        <h3>Code of Conduct</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Respect all participants, mentors, judges, and organizers</li>
          <li>No harassment or discrimination of any kind will be tolerated</li>
          <li>Maintain a collaborative and inclusive environment</li>
          <li>Follow venue rules and maintain cleanliness</li>
          <li>Any violation may result in immediate disqualification</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="rules-category">
        <h3>Intellectual Property</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Teams retain full ownership of their projects</li>
          <li>Organizers reserve the right to showcase projects for promotional purposes</li>
          <li>Patents and commercialization rights belong to the team</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

